    "content": "### Severe Indian Heatwaves\nTemperatures across Northern and Central India regularly cross 45°C in summer, making heat exhaustion and heat stroke high risks.\n\n### Staying Hydrated\nPlain water is not enough during severe sweating. Drink traditional cooling drinks that replenish electrolytes:\n- **Nimbu Pani** (Lemonade with a pinch of salt)\n- **Chaach** (Buttermilk with cumin and salt)\n- **Aam Panna** (Raw mango drink)\n- **Coconut Water** (Nariyal pani)\n\n### Symptoms of Heat Stroke\n- Body temperature of 103°F or higher\n- Hot, red, dry, or damp skin\n- Fast, strong pulse\n- Headache, dizziness, or nausea\n- Fainting or loss of consciousness\n\n### First Aid\nMove the person to a cool area immediately. Apply cool cloths or pour cool water over their body. Do NOT give them fluids to drink if they are vomiting or unconscious. Seek emergency ambulance assistance (102/108) immediately."
